MDL409 (W1 finding 1): regex is a CALLBACK option without the FILENAME flag,
so GOption converts its value to UTF-8 before calling the callback. In the C
locale of the official images, a non-ASCII regex makes mydumper abort at
startup, exit 1.
-- scenario --
tool: mydumper
versions: >= v0.19.1-1
args: --defaults-file /work/mydumper.cnf --host mysql --user e2e --password e2e-password
lint: MDL409
expect config-loaded: true
expect exit: 1
expect stderr-contains: option parsing failed: Invalid byte sequence in conversion input, try --help
expect connected: false
-- mydumper.cnf --
[mydumper]
regex=^app\.(users|zoé)$
